From 512d33598d8743cce683a513c0e2d8a7885447c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hitori-chan <hitori1403@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:19:14 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Add a panel dim action for panel_power_savings beyond
 amdgpu

The Apple silicon display driver takes amdgpu's panel_power_savings ABI
(0 to 4, 0 off) in a group named after it, apple/panel_power_savings, for
the dim macOS applies on battery and in Low Power mode on AC (CoreBrightness:
the SDR luminance times 0.7). The amdgpu action cannot drive it: it probes
by CPU vendor, is opt-in, and grades ABM by battery level on battery only.

panel_dim writes 1 to any connected connector's <driver>/panel_power_savings
but amdgpu's on battery or in power-saver, else 0; on by default, as macOS's
"Slightly dim the display on battery" is. Disabled, or with the daemon
stopping, it writes 0 again, so the panel is never left dimmed.
